  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Printed rules and an agreed temporary ruling are available; any unresolved interpretation can be checked after the evening.\", \"decision\": \"How should a table resolve an unclear rule?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe teacher checks the printed rules when uncertainty arises and proposes a temporary ruling if the text remains unclear. A designated interpreter keeps the interruption short while making the provisional nature of the decision explicit.\nThe player who raised the question reads the relevant printed passage aloud, and the table agrees a temporary ruling. Everyone can inspect the same evidence before consenting to an interpretation for the remainder of that game.\nThe table gives two players a brief rule check while others pause, then accepts their reported interpretation or temporary ruling. The search has clear owners and does not require every player to examine the rulebook simultaneously."
    }
  ],
